block head
    title Colon Polyps - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Colon Polyps
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/colon-polyps/symptoms-causes/syc-20352875") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote A colon polyp is a small clump of cells that forms on the lining of the colon. Most colon polyps are harmless. But over time, some colon polyps can develop into colon cancer. Colon cancer can be fatal when found in its later stages.
